ember","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T15:23:48-08:00","id":1525664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1525644-pcs-arrives-caul-explodes#post1525644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since PCs are bounded to swing the scale one way or the other, have anyone played a game where they help the Lunar retakes the whole Caul? Are there any super magical secrets that get unlocked or is it just business as usual on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty good question - the mythology over the place, that seems to be a major factor motivating both sides in the protacted conflict, would imply that any one side getting control of the Caul's geomancy could have some big effects upon Creation, opening a portal to a realm of existence inacessible for millenia at the least. And even from just an &quot;you got a new territory&quot; perspective, dominating the Caul still means taking over one of the largest islands in Creation (that is not a continent on its own right like the Blessed Isle).<br /> <br /> I also vaguely remember some bits implying there's something funky going on with the place's spirit hierarchies, though i really can't bring up specifics out of my head right now, sorry.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-27T11:19:00-08:00","id":1526015,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s hard to land somewhere between \u201cIt will change Creation forever!\u201d and \u201cIt\u2019s not that important yeah\u201d. Though I wonder if they also have never hold all the cities even in the First Age since the writing seems to be that nobody knows what will happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also vaguely remember some bits implying there's something funky going on with the place's spirit hierarchies, though i really can't bring up specifics out of my head right now, sorry. </div> </div> </div>Yeah it seems like since gods has finally managed to have sex this edition the local Caul\u2019s gods kinda birth a whole lineage of god children who don\u2019t know anything about Yu-shan when the whole island went missing for ages, so they kinda gives the Heaven\u2019s emissary the finger when they went there to bring the wild gods to the fold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-11T01:54:42-08:00","id":1526662,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the info, I will keep it in my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28268,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28268-sanfordhahn","user":"SanfordHahn","date":". 01-10-2024, 03:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28268-sanfordhahn","name":"SanfordHahn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T09:22:14-08:00","id":1527845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1525644-pcs-arrives-caul-explodes#post1525644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"center\"><img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/964950922910376026/1175014075223257168/IMG_9508.jpg?ex=6569b022&amp;is=65573b22&amp;hm=1a5d8a3c1915ced21ea03650222dcfc890e8878a8721b8b0b9369d95e5f6a998&amp;\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/964950922910376026/1175014075223257168/IMG_9508.jpg?ex=6569b022&amp;is=65573b22&amp;hm=1a5d8a3c1915ced21ea03650222dcfc890e8878a8721b8b0b9369d95e5f6a998&amp;\" data-thumb-url=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/964950922910376026/1175014075223257168/IMG_9508.jpg?ex=6569b022&amp;is=65573b22&amp;hm=1a5d8a3c1915ced21ea03650222dcfc890e8878a8721b8b0b9369d95e5f6a998&amp;\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> Since PCs are bounded to swing the scale one way or the other, have anyone played a game where they help the Lunar retakes the whole Caul? Are there any super magical secrets that get unlocked or is it just business as usual on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I ran a short 12 session campaign about a solar doing the pilgrimage on the caul. They had to masquerade as DB's to arrive successfully into the city and trick them into breaking them out of the Lunar seige so they could do the pilgrimage. They found out from Sidereals that INFERNALS were trying to do the pilgrimage. So not only was the island (and lunars) trying to kill them, it was also a race to finish the pilgrimage first. No one really knew what would happen if solars finished the pilgrimage, but Infernals? We had a lot of fun - at the end I said the solars lifted the Great Curse, and purified Abyssals and Infernals currently in creation. OP? But I feel like PC's should have to play for a campaign for 10 IRL years to fix anything in exalted. It is <b>EXALTED</b>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}